        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augusta%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Catlin named Augusta after a memorable visit to Augusta, Georgia, hoping the new town would share its charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augusta%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "On September 18, 1858, Abraham Lincoln visited Augusta, gave a speech, and stayed at Elder James Stark’s home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augusta%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1864, future President James Garfield spoke in Augusta supporting Lincoln during the Civil War.",
